<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>The Shores of Tripoli (The War That Never Was) NATO, 1989</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;The opening moves against Libya by NATO were a great success. The Libyan IADS around Tripoli has been virtually dismantled and the Marines of the 26th MEU have been successfully landed at Zuwara. Initial opposition has been very light and the Marines have driven to within 25 miles of Tripoli.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Meanwhile, NATO's military successes have paid off on the diplomatic front. Egypt has agreed to&amp;nbsp;attack Libya&amp;nbsp;and will begin driving towards Tubruq.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Will the Libyan army collapse under the weight of a two front attack? Or does the "Crazy Colonel" have some tricks up his sleeve?&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This scenario, based upon the book &lt;U&gt;The War That Never Was&lt;/U&gt; by Michael A. Palmer, features heavy use of aircraft supporting ground forces.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
